      trivia: "【He Was a Four-Wheel-Drive Tour Guide】\nBefore entering the cigar trade, James Brown spent more than four years guiding adventure tours by four-wheel drive through the backcountry of Central America.\n【Just Four Pairs at First】\nWhen the factory opened on 9 February 2015 it had only four pairs of rollers and a monthly capacity of about 30,000 cigars, with each pair's daily output limited to 200 to 250 cigars to safeguard quality.\n【Built Not to Look Like a Factory】\nFabrica Oveja Negra is designed to look and feel more like an art studio than a factory. The 2017 facility also houses a retail shop, a lounge and exhibition space.\n【The Black Sheep Honoured Two Years Running】\nCigar Coop's Prime Time Awards named it Factory of the Year in the small/medium factory category in both 2019 and 2020.\n【The Year of the Classic Size】\nAt the 2025 PCA, a 6 × 50 toro was added to Royalty, Lawless and Last Rites — a response, it is said, to the wishes of retailers and consumers."
